00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:17.020
- A long time ago, Iceland didn't exist.

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:18.550
And then these two plates in the middle

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:19.680
of the Atlantic ocean

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:21.770
moved apart and let a bunch of magma

00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:23.290
from under the crust come up.

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:25.900
That magma cooled and that became

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:27.343
an island called Iceland.

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:32.560
In other words, Iceland

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:35.930
is sitting on a literal
crack in the Earth's crust

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:40.163
from which a lot of heat
and magma vents out.

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:43.113
And it's because of this,

00:01:43.113 --> 00:01:46.280
