00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:13.290
So yeah, Iceland is a place
with a lot of hot water.

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:15.020
It's become a part of their culture,

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:17.680
but is it just because it feels good?

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:18.940
- Yeah it feels good.

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:22.670
- The answer is no, it is not
just because it feels good.

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:23.770
So let's get into this.

00:05:23.770 --> 00:05:26.210
Let's talk about what
actually happens to your body

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:28.610
when you immerse it in hot water.

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:30.340
The first thing you have to
understand is that your body

00:05:30.340 --> 00:05:32.760
is obsessed with one temperature.

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:36.150
37 degrees Celsius or 98.6 Fahrenheit.

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:38.350
Your body wants to stay
at that temperature,

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:41.000
especially in your core vital organs.

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:43.100
Your brain, your heart,
your liver, your lungs.

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:44.830
It has to keep it at that temperature.

00:05:44.830 --> 00:05:47.730
If it goes a few degrees
above or below, you're dead.

00:05:47.730 --> 00:05:50.380
And your body has one
really important mechanism

00:05:50.380 --> 00:05:53.690
for keeping itself cool,
when it's too hot outside.

00:05:53.690 --> 00:05:56.040
Or hot, when it's too cold outside.

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:58.453
And that very important
mechanism is blood.

00:05:59.570 --> 00:06:01.380
So let's say you jump
into super hot water,

00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:04.010
40 degrees Celsius,
104 degrees Fahrenheit.

00:06:04.010 --> 00:06:05.160
Your body freaks out a little bit.

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:05.993
It's like, whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:06:05.993 --> 00:06:08.030
This ambient temperature is way hotter

00:06:08.030 --> 00:06:10.950
than what we are used
too and what we want.

00:06:10.950 --> 00:06:13.520
So it immediately gets to
work, cooling yourself down.

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:14.710
And it uses blood to do this.

00:06:14.710 --> 00:06:16.520
It says, get all of the blood

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:18.140
out of this center of the body,

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:19.360
where all the important organs are,

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:21.180
send them out to the extremities.

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:24.140
Let the fingers and the legs
and the calf muscles get hot.

00:06:24.140 --> 00:06:25.720
Don't let the heart get hot.

00:06:25.720 --> 00:06:28.280
So your heart pumps and your blood vessels

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:31.240
start pulsing a little
bit to push that blood

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:33.110
out into different parts of your body.

00:06:33.110 --> 00:06:33.943
Your blood vessels,

00:06:33.943 --> 00:06:36.860
literally open up to allow this to happen.

00:06:36.860 --> 00:06:38.940
Like they like open up to make it easier

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:41.930
for the blood to get the
hell out of the heart

00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:43.690
and out to the extremities.

00:06:43.690 --> 00:06:45.530
And it works, it works really wonderfully.

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:47.708
And honestly, it feels really good.

00:06:47.708 --> 00:06:50.291
(upbeat music)

00:06:57.730 --> 00:07:00.480
If you dip your body
in hot water regularly,

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:02.420
you are giving the body,

00:07:02.420 --> 00:07:04.980
a chance to push blood
out to all of these places

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:07.690
that don't get a lot of
blood most of the time.

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:09.380
Mix that with the fact
that these hot Springs

00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:10.870
are usually loaded with minerals

00:07:10.870 --> 00:07:12.970
that are really good for the body.

00:07:12.970 --> 00:07:14.100
And as you soak in them,

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:16.390
you absorb them and that
helps your body too.

00:07:16.390 --> 00:07:19.450
So it's no surprise to
me that not only Iceland,

00:07:19.450 --> 00:07:22.090
but all sorts of cultures
all around the world

00:07:22.090 --> 00:07:25.859
have discovered that soaking
in hot water is a good thing.

