00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:14.740
because he sort of has
this guru vibe going on.

00:12:14.740 --> 00:12:16.770
Where he's like this
wild, crazy character.

00:12:16.770 --> 00:12:18.850
And like he has this wild, new methods.

00:12:18.850 --> 00:12:20.860
That's going to solve your world.

00:12:20.860 --> 00:12:23.300
However, I started looking into

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:27.620
study after study, after
study, after study.

00:12:27.620 --> 00:12:31.000
About cold water and what
it does to our bodies.

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:31.900
And I have to say,

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:37.740
despite my deep skepticism
of Wim Hof is the guru

00:12:37.740 --> 00:12:40.790
and his followers as just another

00:12:40.790 --> 00:12:43.863
sort of like trendy new
age wellness business.

00:12:44.780 --> 00:12:45.764
I'm convinced.

00:12:45.764 --> 00:12:48.347
(upbeat music)

00:13:12.550 --> 00:13:16.670
It turns out that the benefit
of going into cold water

00:13:16.670 --> 00:13:19.560
is actually incredibly well-documented.

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:21.770
Through randomized controlled studies

00:13:21.770 --> 00:13:23.870
that have nothing to do with Wim Hof.

00:13:23.870 --> 00:13:28.870
They studied people who go
swimming in ice water in Finland.

00:13:29.050 --> 00:13:32.380
And found that these
people are way stronger,

00:13:32.380 --> 00:13:37.380
more resilient, less prone
to anxiety, depression,

00:13:37.420 --> 00:13:40.510
their bodies function more effectively.

00:13:40.510 --> 00:13:42.020
And the craziest part,

00:13:42.020 --> 00:13:44.180
the one that blows my
mind is they discovered

00:13:44.180 --> 00:13:46.010
that when you go into cold water,

00:13:46.010 --> 00:13:48.910
your body actually creates
more white blood cells.

00:13:48.910 --> 00:13:51.800
The defense cells that
help with your immunity.

00:13:51.800 --> 00:13:53.610
So people who dip in cold water actually

00:13:53.610 --> 00:13:55.970
have stronger immune systems.

00:13:55.970 --> 00:13:58.670
There's absolutely something to this.

00:13:58.670 --> 00:14:00.610
And as I've scrutinized
it and looked into it

00:14:00.610 --> 00:14:02.123
and done it myself.

00:14:04.490 --> 00:14:08.100
I've learned that it's
actually pretty compelling

00:14:08.100 --> 00:14:09.880
and something that I
feel like I'm probably

00:14:09.880 --> 00:14:13.120
going to start doing
more and more in my life.

00:14:13.120 --> 00:14:17.330
The data is there, it's
real, it is very compelling.

00:14:17.330 --> 00:14:18.460
And here's the deal.

00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:19.560
As I've been here in Iceland,

00:14:19.560 --> 00:14:21.190
I've been experimenting with this.

00:14:21.190 --> 00:14:23.213
I've been going into cold water.

00:14:23.213 --> 00:14:26.720
It's been horrendous,
but it's been amazing.

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:28.770
There's this feeling you
get when you come out of it,

00:14:28.770 --> 00:14:30.770
where you're just like in this euphoria.

00:14:32.326 --> 00:14:34.140
I freaking love Iceland.

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:37.470
So my little adventure into hot water,

00:14:37.470 --> 00:14:39.860
into natural hot Springs.

00:14:39.860 --> 00:14:43.030
Into cold water has
been really interesting.

00:14:43.030 --> 00:14:44.680
Not just because it feels good,

00:14:44.680 --> 00:14:47.370
but because it has really amazing

00:14:47.370 --> 00:14:50.650
health benefits that people caught onto.

00:14:50.650 --> 00:14:53.020
And that's why they made
it a part of their culture.

00:14:53.020 --> 00:14:54.870
Because it helped people live better.

